Diagnostic:

(a) ModuleStateUnblocked user fires on t2 from try_unblock_locked (inside
    notify_typecheck_done(helper)) — the H5 site. H5 gate is active:
    after emission, user is NOT pushed into typecheck_first (the
    push suppression is silent-in-trace; the absence of
    ModuleStateTypechecking user on t2 after this point proves the
    gate fired).

(b) NO ModuleStateTypechecking user on t2 in this window (compare
    pre-fix post-fix-run-35062ca.log line 36:
    "ts=14477417 thr=ThreadId(2)/1 ModuleStateTypechecking module=user"
    which is the pinning H5 signature; absent here).

(c) IsTypecheckedHit helper pool=4 + RegisterImportsLookup helper on
    t1 — the REPL-eval thread is the SOLE consumer of
    symbol_tables[helper] in the hot path. Exactly per /arch §3d'
    condition (c).

(d) Lookup fails despite pool=4 (TypecheckDone). t2 published helper's
    symbol_tables entry before emitting ModuleStateTypechecked at
    ts=16910791; t1 observed pool=TypecheckDone at ts=16969833 (+59 µs
    later, after condvar wake) but the helper-val symbol read fails.
    This is consistent with an H6 data-plane partial-visibility
    signature — symbol_tables[helper] mutation is visible to t1 via
    the scheduler mutex but the underlying HashMap entry may be in a
    transient state from t2's insertion (or the insertion happens
    AFTER the ModuleStateTypechecked event's scheduler-state update,
    so the condvar wake leads t1 to read before t2's data-plane
    publish). /arch §7.8 named this residue as "H1-adjacent data-plane
    partial-visibility signature, strictly downstream of the race-to-
    claim that H5 names". H5 fix does not address it (and was not
    intended to); deferred to S62 H6 slice.

