========================
/arch 3d' condition checklist:
========================

(1) Caller audit — DONE, documented at top of register_dep_for_eval
    in src/session_v4.rs. Only register_dep_for_eval calls
    wait_module_inmem_complete_blocking (one test has a comment
    noting it avoids the call).
(2) Lock discipline — set_eval_in_flight takes self.lock() (scheduler
    state lock), same lock try_unblock_locked's caller holds. No
    atomics, no separate mutex.
(3) Narrow scope — the RAII guard spans register_dep_for_eval from
    just after computing `caller` through function exit. This is
    /arch's alternative "Recommendation" option 1 from §3d' (set at
    function entry after caller is computed). The narrower variant
    (around just wait_module_inmem_complete_blocking) was TRIED FIRST
    and was validated-insufficient: t2 completed helper and called
    try_unblock_locked(user) with eval_in_flight=false BEFORE t1
    reached the wait, resulting in set_eval_in_flight firing on a
    user that was already TypecheckWorking. The function-entry scope
    is required to win the race. See §3e' — H5 fix implementation
    notes (this doc).
(4) Observability — RepublishFromSymbolTable and RegisterImportsLookup
    continue to fire at their existing sites (worker.rs:1242-1245 and
    session_v4.rs:1255-1258). ModuleStateUnblocked also continues to
    fire from try_unblock_locked (always — including in the flag-
    gated path). No new trace tags added.
